TYPES.md §5.2, §1: a field item in a table literal is E3320, once: the misplaced item has no expected type, so a literal it holds is not judged again (no E3305).
-- a/a.canon --
package a

local record R {
  a: Int
}

local let t: table R = { x { a: 1 }, y: { b: {} } }
-- findings.txt --
error[E3320]  a/a.canon:7:38
  field items are not allowed in table literals

1 error, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
